    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dante was renamed in 1903 after developer Stilson Hutchins’ associate, William Joseph Dante, replacing its original name of Turkey Foot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dhr.virginia.gov/historic-registers/083-5153/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s early growth exploded in the 1900s when the Clinchfield Coal Corporation turned Dante into a company coal town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dante%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1912 tunnel, the Sandy Ridge Tunnel, let the Clinchfield Railroad reach Elkhorn City, Kentucky, extending its reach northward.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dante%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2016, residents revived the town’s future by forming the Dante Community Association to pursue revitalization and grant funding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
